<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-1459] Zeppelin JDBC URL properties mangled</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1459</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m using Phoenix&apos;s thin client which needs to include a property at the end of the JDBC URL.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I can set the driver up correctly in the Interpreter menu, and the first paragraph runs successfully:&lt;br/&gt;
%jdbc(phoenix) select count&lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/emoticons/star_yellow.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt; from system.catalog&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But any paragraphs beyond the first fail with &quot;No suitable driver found errors.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I added debug statements to dump the interpreter properties.&lt;/p&gt;

